  "discussion": {
    "headline": "typical august pattern with several shower chances through the weekend",
    "dateLine": "11:30 a.m. Tuesday, August 18, 2026",
    "excerpt": "The third week of August kicked off on a partly sunny, hot and humid note in advance of a weak cold front. High temperatures reached the upper 80s to low 90s Monday afternoon with dewpoints in the low-to-mid 70s and peak heat indices in the mid 90s. The front triggered scattered showers and a few drenching thunderstorms across the Lower Susquehanna Valley between 1-8 PM, but there were only a few reports of wind damage in Berks County. …",
